      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T23:34:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s a real hang, the wdt triggers whether it\u0027s 2.5 or 1.6 sec.\n\nOne option is to keep the bar high (\u003d1.6) during development (CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED) and relax the bar in production.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "956506d9e4af233e769557316734a3ebc8f480f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c188b0e6_9e96d366",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-13T16:26:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think a separate default with CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED is needed.  \nFalse positives even during board bring-up are time consuming to reproduce and debug.",
      "parentUuid": "e19fcb86_87d7401f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "956506d9e4af233e769557316734a3ebc8f480f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef8d9ac3_b3302601",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T16:25:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that\u0027s only true if you consider it just preventing hard hangs, but it could lead to performance cases if we leave it at the higher threshold. For example, a tight loop is encountered that doesn\u0027t trigger the WDG, but maybe causes PD packets to be late or something.",
      "parentUuid": "c188b0e6_9e96d366",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "956506d9e4af233e769557316734a3ebc8f480f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e099dc5_2a3c1797",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T21:09:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A WDT is a very blunt tool for detecting task performance issues. IMO, we need separate tooling designed for this scenario, e.g. metrics collection or performance based tests.\n\nIf we want to hold off on this CL until we have other tools in place, that\u0027s fine. I can create some blocker bugs.",
      "parentUuid": "ef8d9ac3_b3302601",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "956506d9e4af233e769557316734a3ebc8f480f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "638a6066_9ab87aac",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-14T00:12:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m ok with this change if we have other ways to detect \u0026 collect wdt warning/crashes. I\u0027m worried we\u0027ll see fewer reports from dogfooders because they\u0027re ok to see slowness in whatever the EC does.",
      "revId": "956506d9e4af233e769557316734a3ebc8f480f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
